        "body": "Telmatosaurus transsylvanicus was described by Franz Baron Nopcsa in 1900 from material collected in Transylvania (now Romania). Nopcsa, an aristocratic Hungarian-Romanian palaeontologist, was a pioneer in studying European dinosaurs and was among the first to propose that many Hateg Basin dinosaurs were island dwarfs. The genus name references its presumed swampy habitat; the species name refers to Transylvania, the historical region where the fossils were found."
