        "body": "At approximately 5 metres, Telmatosaurus is considerably smaller than its closest continental relatives, which routinely exceeded 10 metres. This size reduction is attributed to insular dwarfism — the evolutionary reduction of body size in island populations where resource availability is limited and predation pressure may be relaxed. Nopcsa himself was the first to propose this explanation for the Hateg fauna, a remarkably prescient insight for the early 20th century."
